</section>
<section id="S5.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.3 </span>Evaluator Reliability Validation</h3>

<div id="S5.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To validate our framework, we measure agreement with expert human judgments on proof validity and compare against reference-based LLM-as-a-Judge baselines. As shown in Table <a href="#S5.T3" title="Table 3 ‣ 5.2 Cognitive Evaluation Metrics ‣ 5 Neuro-Symbolic Evaluation Framework ‣ LogicGraph : Benchmarking Multi-Path Logical Reasoning via Neuro-Symbolic Generation and Verification" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>, our reference-free neuro-symbolic evaluator (with Prover9) is robust across backbone LLMs: both the Gemini-2.5-Flash and DeepSeek-V3.2-Exp versions outperform reference-based LLM-as-a-Judge baselines, with DeepSeek-V3.2-Exp achieving the highest agreement. This suggests symbolic verification reduces false positives from fluent-but-invalid traces.</p>
</div>
